WEBVTT

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:08.080
Yes, she will sing
to those who hear

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:14.720
And in her song,
all magic flows

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:19.680
But can you brave
what you most fear?

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:27.040
Can you face
what the river knows?

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:32.320
Where the Northwind

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:35.520
Meets the sea

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.800
There's a mother

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.960
Full of memory

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:46.680
Come, my darling,
homeward bound

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.080
When all is lost

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:55.520
Then all is found

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:01.040
-Your Majesty.
-Oh! (GRUNTS)

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:02.240
They're ready.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:03.520
(CHUCKLES)

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:04.720
Excuse me.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:06.480
I'm coming.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:09.560
-(ANGELIC VOICE VOCALIZING)
-(GASPS)

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:12.240
-Do you hear that?
-(VOCALIZING STOPS)

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:13.320
What?

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:16.440
Never mind.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:23.800
(WIND WHISTLING)

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:32.720
(SHUDDERS)

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:33.800
(GASPS)

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:39.280
(CHUCKLES) Enjoying
your new permafrost, Olaf?

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:42.160
I'm just living the dream,
Anna. (SIGHS)

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:43.280
How I wish

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:44.840
-this could last forever.
-Mmm.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.360
And yet, change mocks us
with her beauty.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:49.520
What's that?

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:51.640
Forgive me.
Maturity is making me poetic.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:52.720
(FLAPS LIPS)

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.640
Tell me, you're older
and thus all-knowing...

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.760
do you ever worry
about the notion that...

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:58.480
nothing is permanent?

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:00.440
Uh... No.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:01.760
Really?

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:04.560
Wow, I can't wait until
I'm ancient like you...

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:07.360
so I don't have to worry
about important things.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.640
That's not what I mean.

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:11.680
I don't worry because...

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:15.520
well, I have you and Elsa
and Kristoff and Sven...

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:18.000
and the gates are open wide...

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:19.880
and I'm not alone anymore.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:20.960
(MUSIC PLAYING)

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:24.120
(SINGING) Yes, the wind blows
a little bit colder

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:26.040
And we're all getting older

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:31.320
And the clouds are moving on
With every autumn breeze

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:34.160
Peter Pumpkin
just became fertilizer

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.800
And my leaf's a little sadder
and wiser

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.320
That's why I rely
on certain certainties

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:45.560
Yes, some things never change

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:47.880
Like the feel
of your hand in mine

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:50.640
Some things stay the same

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.760
Like how we get along
just fine

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:55.880
Like an old stone wall
that'll never fall

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:58.600
Some things are always true!

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:00.000
(OLAF LAUGHING)

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:03.280
Some things never change

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:06.640
Like how
I'm holding on tight to you

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:08.240
(OLAF LAUGHING)

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:12.760
The leaves are already falling

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.560
Sven, it feels
like the future is calling

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:17.040
Are you telling me tonight

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.560
You're gonna get down
on one knee?

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.640
Yeah, but I'm really bad
at planning these things out

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:26.320
Like candlelight
and pulling of rings out

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:31.120
Maybe you should leave
all the romantic stuff to me!

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:34.720
Yeah, some things never change

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:37.160
Like the love
that I feel for her

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:40.000
Some things stay the same

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:42.240
Like how reindeers are easier

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.160
But if I commit
and I go for it

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:48.040
I'll know what to say and do!

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:49.240
Right?

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:52.720
Some things never change

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:55.200
Sven, the pressure
is all on you

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:57.320
(ANNA AND OLAF LAUGHING)

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:02.240
The winds are restless

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:05.480
Could that be why
I'm hearing this call?

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.240
Is something coming?

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:10.360
I'm not sure
I want things to change at all

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:12.200
These days are precious

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:15.120
Can't let them slip away

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:18.480
I can't freeze this moment

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:24.480
But I can still go out
and seize this day!

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.000
Oh! (CHUCKLES)

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:31.400
(LAUGHING)

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.040
(ALL VOCALIZING)

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:40.320
The wind blows
a little bit colder

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:43.040
And you all look
a little bit older

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:44.920
It's time to count
our blessings

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:48.520
Beneath an autumn sky

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:51.360
We'll always live
in a kingdom of plenty

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:54.040
That stands
for the good of the many!

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:58.280
And I promise you the flag of
Arendelle will always fly!

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.920
Our flag will always fly!

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:05.080
Our flag will always fly
Our flag will always fly

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:08.080
Some things never change

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:10.240
Turn around
and the time has flown

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:13.520
Some things stay the same

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:15.720
Though the future
remains unknown

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:18.480
May our good luck last
May our past be past

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:22.400
Time's moving fast, it's true

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:25.600
Some things never change

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:29.360
And I'm holding on tight
to you

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:30.920
Holding on tight to you

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:35.240
-Holding on tight to you
-Holding on tight to you

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:43.120
I'm holding on tight to you

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:47.000
(BELL RINGS) (BELL RINGS)

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.800
(GROWLING)

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:50.960
KRISTOFF: Uh, okay.
Um, lion?

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:52.120
Grizzly bear?

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.240
-Uh, monster?
-Brown bear?

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:54.560
-Angry face?
-Black bear?

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:55.720
-KRISTOFF: Uh...
-Hans?

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:58.000
-(GRUNTS ENCOURAGINGLY)
-Unredeemable monster?

00:05:58.080 --> 00:05:59.120
Greatest mistake of your life?

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:00.480
Wouldn't even kiss you?

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:01.560
-(BELL RINGS)
-(SVEN MOANS)

00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:02.880
Villain!

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.280
ALL: Oh!

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:05.400
We all kind of got it.

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:06.680
Okay, Olaf, you're up.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:07.840
Okay.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:09.680
So much easier
now that I can read.

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:10.800
SVEN: Mm.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:12.920
Lightning round,
boys against girls.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.000
(BELL RINGS)

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:15.880
KRISTOFF: Okay, I'm ready,
I'm ready. Go.

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:17.880
Unicorn.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:19.080
Ice cream!

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:20.760
-Castle! Oaken!
-(OLAF WHISTLES)

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:22.560
Teapot! Mouse!

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:24.280
Oh! Elsa!

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:25.920
-(BELL RINGS)
-(LAUGHING)

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.160
I don't think
Olaf should get to rearrange.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:29.920
Doesn't matter. This is gonna
be a cinch. (CRACKS KNUCKLES)

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.560
-(SVEN GRUNTS)
-Two sisters, one mind.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:34.320
-Thank you.
-ANNA: Okay.

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:35.680
-Here we go.
-(BELL RINGS)

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:37.400
You got this, Elsa.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:39.280
ELSA: Hmm.
ANNA: Anytime.

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:40.920
Just do it with your body.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:42.160
Uh, nothing?

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:44.680
Air? Tree? People?

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:46.160
Treeple?
Oh, that's not a word.

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:48.160
-Oh, shovel boy? Teeth?
-(ELSA SIGHS)

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:49.280
Oh! Doing the dishes?

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:50.440
-Polar bear?
-Hey.

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:51.760
-Sorry.
-Uh... Ugh.

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:52.880
ANNA: You gotta
give me something.

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:55.120
-Um... (GASPS)
-(ANGELIC VOICE VOCALIZING)

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:57.000
ANNA: Oh! Uh, alarmed?

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:58.880
-(MUFFLED) Distracted?
-(ELSA PANTING)

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:01.440
Um, worried?
Panicking? Disturbed?

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:02.760
Oh, come on,
you definitely

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:04.480
-look disturbed. (GROANS)
-(BELL RINGS)

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:05.600
-We won.
-(OLAF GIGGLES)

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:06.680
Rematch?

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:09.760
Oh, you know what?
I think I'll turn in.

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:10.920
Are you okay?

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:13.160
ELSA: Just... Just tired.
(CHUCKLES)

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:14.560
Good night.

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:16.040
-(YAWNS) Yeah, I'm tired, too.
-(SVEN YAWNS)

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:18.200
And Sven promised to read me
a bedtime story.

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:19.840
Didn't you, Sven?

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.040
(MIMICS SVEN) Did I?

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:23.160
Oh, you do the best voices!

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:25.760
Like when you pretend to be
Kristoff, and you're like...

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:27.760
(MIMICS KRISTOFF) "I just
need to go talk to some rocks

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:29.200
"about my childhood
and stuff."

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:30.880
(IN NORMAL VOICE)
Um, how about you guys

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:32.560
start without me?

